    "body": "Independent review (Codex nonauthor subagent) of head e1dbc026b851d13bf50d6d01abe2d4e60395d379\n\nRELAYED REVIEW, not a formal GitHub approval. Reviewer /root/save043_architect independently reviewed all 12 changed files against base e0ee34d356d61c42e9809305647415c103e3cf84 and wrote no shipped 048 code. Verdict: PASS, no actionable P1/P2 findings.\n\nActual checks: core 836, wording 74, headless UI 1,208, unchanged radial 58, playfield 94, fleet 78, expedition 47, campaign 52, lock warning 14, and native UI 1,412. Total: 3,873 checks, zero failures. Import, registry validation of 277 suites, and guidance with 10 regression tests also passed. There are 28 native captures across both Fold7 shapes at 150% text size. An additional external refresh, resize, inverse-hit and off-switch probe passed 764 checks. Root verified raw result records, logs and every capture hash and dimension.\n\nInitial import/core began on fa13dbd7. Core completed across the final three-line RESUME-only change; the reviewer proved game/scripts byte-identical to final e1dbc026. All later suites and final import ran on the final head. No shipped assertions changed. Original external exact-floating-equality probe failures (764 checks, 8 failures) and an incorrect-path diagnostic remain archived. Measured rounding was 0.00006103515625 pixels; all geometry, overlap, target-size, hit and snapshot assertions already passed. The corrected external diagnostic uses a justified subpixel threshold. These probe and runner failures are preserved and explained.\n\nFull attributable assessment, commands, timings, raw logs and captures: https://github.com/pemunson90-cmd/Siren-s-Song/tree/2cc0ac23/evidence/048-windows-20261025 . Root reopened and verified all 63 independent ZIP members, SHA256 2c4577378ac8ef092c305bf14d599250c58a65945c3594417cdcbdd5c9803e59.\n\nHosted run 40249328277 has passed guidance; game-smoke remains pending as a separate merge gate. Desktop technical verification only, not full local scenario coverage, blind-player or phone acceptance.",
